{#- Legacy standalone DeepSeek-V4.1 Jinja export. Maya's server renders DeepSeek with serve/ds41_encoding.py,
    pinned to revision 1bae0e1088993b9b82de08f59de5be5a34e42170 of deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017.
    This export covers ordinary chat/tools only; see docs/deepseek-prompt-format.md for its conformance limits.
    DeepSeek-V4.1's prompt format (the model repo's encoding/encoding.py), approximated in Jinja.
    Turns: <｜User｜> ... <｜Assistant｜> (reasoning</think>)answer<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>.  Thinking mode ends the prompt
    with <think> and starts with a reasoning-effort line (low 50, high 75, max 100); chat mode ends it with </think>.
    Tool results (role "tool") are <tool_result> blocks of a user turn, merged with the user messages around them;
    tool calls are DSML blocks; the tools are listed in the system turn.  Earlier turns keep their reasoning only when
    tools are given (encoding.py's drop_thinking).  A picture in a message's content list is its placeholder
    <｜deepseek_image｜>, a block of its own between the text blocks (the server expands it into the picture's span). -#}
{%- set thinking = enable_thinking is not defined or enable_thinking -%}
{%- set efforts = {'low': 50, 'medium': 75, 'high': 75, 'xhigh': 100, 'max': 100} -%}
{%- if reasoning_effort is defined and reasoning_effort is number -%}
{%- set budget = reasoning_effort -%}
{%- elif reasoning_effort is defined and reasoning_effort in efforts -%}
{%- set budget = efforts[reasoning_effort] -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set budget = 75 -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set has_tools = tools is defined and tools is not none and tools | length > 0 -%}
{%- set keep = has_tools -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(last_user=-1, schemas='') -%}
{%- if has_tools -%}{%- for t in tools -%}{%- set ns.schemas = ns.schemas ~ (t | tojson) ~ ('' if loop.last else '\n') -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- for m in messages -%}{%- if m.role == 'user' -%}{%- set ns.last_user = loop.index0 -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- macro text(c) -%}
{%- if c is string -%}{{ c }}{%- elif c is iterable -%}
{%- for p in c if p.type in ['text', 'image'] -%}{%- if not loop.first -%}{{ '\n\n' }}{%- endif -%}{{ p.text if p.type == 'text' else '<｜deepseek_image｜>' }}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro tools_block() -%}
## Tools

You have access to a set of tools to help answer the user's question. You can invoke tools by writing a "<｜DSML｜ calls>" block like the following:

<｜DSML｜ calls>
<｜DSML｜ invoke name="$TOOL_NAME">
<｜DSML｜ parameter name="$PARAMETER_NAME" string="true|false">$PARAMETER_VALUE</｜DSML｜ parameter>
...
</｜DSML｜ invoke>
<｜DSML｜ invoke name="$TOOL_NAME2">
...
</｜DSML｜ invoke>
</｜DSML｜ calls>

String parameters should be specified as is and set `string="true"`. For all other types (numbers, booleans, arrays, objects), pass the value in JSON format and set `string="false"`.

If thinking_mode is enabled (triggered by <think>), you MUST output your complete reasoning inside <think>...</think> BEFORE any tool calls or final response.

Otherwise, output directly after </think> with tool calls or final response.

### Available Tool Schemas

{{ ns.schemas }}

You MUST strictly follow the above defined tool name and parameter schemas to invoke tool calls.
{% endmacro -%}
{{- '<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- set effort_line = ('Reasoning Effort: ' ~ budget ~ ' (range 1-100, the higher the value, the more thorough the reasoning)\n\n') if thinking else '' -%}
{%- if messages and messages[0].role == 'system' -%}
{{- '<｜System｜>' ~ effort_line ~ text(messages[0].content) -}}
{%- if has_tools -%}{{- '\n\n' ~ tools_block() -}}{%- endif -%}
{%- elif has_tools -%}
{{- '<｜System｜>' ~ effort_line ~ '\n\n' ~ tools_block() -}}
{%- elif thinking -%}
{{- '<｜System｜>' ~ effort_line -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- for m in messages -%}
{%- set i = loop.index0 -%}
{%- set prev = messages[i - 1].role if i > 0 else '' -%}
{%- set next = messages[i + 1].role if i + 1 < messages | length else '' -%}
{%- if m.role == 'system' and i == 0 -%}
{%- elif m.role in ['user', 'tool', 'system'] -%}
{%- if prev in ['user', 'tool'] or (prev == 'system' and i - 1 > 0) -%}{{- '\n\n' -}}{%- else -%}{{- '<｜User｜>' -}}{%- endif -%}
{%- if m.role == 'tool' -%}{{- '<tool_result>' ~ text(m.content) ~ '</tool_result>' -}}{%- else -%}{{- text(m.content) -}}{%- endif -%}
{%- if next not in ['user', 'tool', 'system'] -%}
{%- if thinking and (keep or i >= ns.last_user) -%}{{- '<｜Assistant｜><think>' -}}{%- else -%}{{- '<｜Assistant｜></think>' -}}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif m.role == 'assistant' -%}
{%- if thinking and (keep or i > ns.last_user) -%}{{- (m.reasoning_content or '') ~ '</think>' -}}{%- endif -%}
{{- text(m.content) -}}
{%- if m.tool_calls -%}
{{- '\n\n<｜DSML｜ calls>\n' -}}
{%- for c in m.tool_calls -%}
{%- set f = c.function if c.function is defined else c -%}
{{- '<｜DSML｜ invoke name="' ~ f.name ~ '">\n' -}}
{%- for k, v in (f.arguments or {}).items() -%}
{{- '<｜DSML｜ parameter name="' ~ k ~ '" string="' ~ ('true' if v is string else 'false') ~ '">' ~ (v if v is string else v | tojson) ~ '</｜DSML｜ parameter>' -}}
{%- if not loop.last -%}{{- '\n' -}}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- '\n</｜DSML｜ invoke>' -}}{%- if not loop.last -%}{{- '\n' -}}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- '\n</｜DSML｜ calls>' -}}
{%- endif -%}
{{- '<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
